                    "text": "`indicator` shows a dot (`true`) or a count (a number above 0, floored; `0`, negatives, `NaN`, `false` and `null` hide it) on the top-end corner, anchored at 0.146 × the button height so it sits on the corner arc of every type, size and shape; a count above `indicatorMax` (default 99) reads `{max}+`. It uses `--sd-{indicatorColor}` (default `error`) with its `-contrast` text and a 2px ring of the new `--sd-button-indicator-ring` token (`var(--sd-surface)`), turns grey on a disabled button, stays while loading, and never changes the button size. Under forced colors it is drawn in `CanvasText` with a `Canvas` ring (`GrayText` when disabled), so the dot stays visible. It is a sibling of the native button, `aria-hidden`; `indicatorLabel` is a visually hidden text added to the button's `aria-describedby`. See `sd-button.md`, \"Indicator\".",
