            "key": "select-autocomplete",
            "title": "Select, Autocomplete",
            "level": 4,
            "anchor": "release-3-2-fixed-select-autocomplete",
            "markdown": "- Select, Autocomplete and the other outlined `size=\"sm\"` fields: the resting floating label shares the 24px line height of the value, so it sits on the same pixel row as the placeholder and the selected value on every OS.\n  - On Windows it was 1px lower: Chrome floors the half-leading of the value line, and Roboto is 17px tall there (16px on Linux and macOS). The old `sm` label rule targeted a Material 2 class and never applied.",
