                    "text": "The row used to lay the translated label and the raw code side by side, so inside an `<sd-table>` inline column filter — where the panel is only as wide as the column — a long label such as `Lớn hơn, hoặc bằng` wrapped onto a second line and the rows ended up at different heights. The label now owns the first line (weight 400, `nowrap`) and the code the second, still muted grey 11px monospace; `mat-menu-item`'s single-line box is released (`min-height: 0`, `height: auto`, `line-height: normal`) so the second line is not cropped. Measured on the number-operator set: the panel narrows from 304px to 235px and rows go from 48px to 46px, because the label no longer shares its line with the code.",
